What caused the error (two bugs, two sessions)
Bug 1 — Fixed last session (API: wrong upload directory + outside try-catch)

pages/api/upload.js wrote uploaded files to process.cwd()/uploads. On Vercel's serverless runtime, process.cwd() is a read-only filesystem path, so fs.mkdirSync() threw an EACCES error. Because that call was outside the try-catch, Next.js returned a raw HTML 500 page instead of JSON. Axios then got back HTML, err.response?.data?.error was undefined, and the fallback message appeared:

    "Failed to upload document. Please try again."

Fix: Use os.tmpdir() (/tmp, always writable) and move everything inside the try-catch.
Bug 2 — Fixed this session (Frontend: explicit Content-Type without boundary)

DocumentUpload.js set headers: { 'Content-Type': 'multipart/form-data' } on the axios POST. The XMLHttpRequest spec (§4.5.6) says: "If Content-Type is already in the author request headers, the Content-Type extracted from the FormData body (which includes the boundary) is not appended." The result: the server received a multipart request with no boundary, formidable threw "bad content-type header, no multipart boundary", and the upload failed.

Fix: Removed the explicit headers override entirely (3 lines deleted). Axios automatically sets Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=... when the body is a FormData object.
